@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<section class="section-space">
    <div class="container booking-container">
        <h1 class="page-title">Patient data in this prototype</h1>
        <p>Confirming an appointment stores your name, phone number, email, specialty, doctor, appointment time and booking status in the local clinic database. Patient accounts are stored in the same database using ASP.NET Core Identity, which hashes passwords.</p>
        <p>Booking details are not saved while moving between the booking steps. No confirmation emails are sent. Signed-in patients can view and cancel appointments matching their account email.</p>
        <p>Confirming creates a Pending appointment and a Stripe-hosted test checkout for an AED 100 consultation deposit. The database stores the checkout session ID. Stripe receives the appointment reference and handles payment details on its own website; the clinic application does not receive card numbers. Your appointment becomes Booked only after server-side payment verification.</p>
        <div class="alert alert-warning">This is a development prototype. Email ownership is not verified yet. Use sample information only, not real patient data.</div>
        <p>A clinic-specific privacy policy, data-retention rules and verified email ownership must be implemented before public use.</p>
    </div>
</section>
